"2024-11-26T19:15:48.475Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2024-11-26t19:15:48.475z"},{"subject":"CVE-2024-8676","predicate":"date-updated","object":"2026-11-05T14:44:43.958Z","source":"cve","object_type":"date","object_canonical":"2026-11-05t14:44:43.958z"},{"subject":"CVE-2024-8676","predicate":"description","object":"A vulnerability was found in CRI-O, where it can be requested to take a checkpoint archive of a container and later be asked to restore it. When it does that restoration, it attempts to restore the mounts from the restore archive instead of the pod request. As a result, the validations run on the pod spec, verifying that the pod has access to the mounts it specifies are not applicable to a restored container. This flaw allows a malicious user to trick CRI-O into restoring a pod that doesn't have access to host mounts. The user needs access to the kubelet or cri-o socket to call the restore endpoint and trigger the restore.","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"a vulnerability was found in cri-o, where it can be requested to take a checkpoint archive of a container and later be asked to restore it. when it does that restoration, it attempts to restore the mounts from the restore archive instead of the pod request. as a result, the validations run on the pod spec, verifying that the pod has access to the mounts it specifies are not applicable to a restored container. this flaw allows a malicious user to trick cri-o into restoring a pod that doesn't have access to host mounts. the user needs access to the kubelet or cri-o socket to call the restore endpoint and trigger the restore."},{"subject":"CVE-2024-8676","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform 4.15","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat openshift container platform 4.15"},{"subject":"CVE-2024-8676","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform 4.16","source":"cve","object_ty